# Reusability and Theme Consistency

## Theme Palette First

- Prefer semantic theme tokens and CSS variables over hardcoded colors (for example: `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `border-border-subtle`).
- Keep light/dark behavior driven by shared theme variables so components adapt automatically without per-page overrides.
- When adjusting styles, reuse existing palette tokens before introducing new color values.

## Reusable Component Architecture

- Prioritize reusable and modular code over one-off page-specific implementations.
- Centralize base behavior and styling in shared root components (for example `src/components/ui/button.tsx`), and keep consumer overrides minimal.
- If multiple features need the same UI/interaction pattern, extract or extend a shared component instead of duplicating logic.
- Favor small, composable APIs (`variant`, `size`, `className`) that keep component usage consistent and maintainable.

## Maintainability Standard

- Optimize for long-term maintainability: one source of truth for core UI patterns, minimal duplication, predictable theming.
- New styling decisions should strengthen the reusable template codebase, not fragment it.
